# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules. Copied verbatim into the site root at build
# time (see eleventy.config.js) and read by Pages itself — this file does
# nothing locally and nothing on the GitHub Pages mirror.
#
# Why: the old WordPress site at this domain used flat, post-name permalinks
# (/start-with-your-audience/). The Eleventy site nests posts under /posts/,
# so every inbound link and search result pointing at an old URL 404s without
# these. Source URLs were recovered from the Internet Archive's CDX index for
# jacobcorcoran.com and confirmed to have returned 200 on the old site.
#
# Format: <from> <to> <status>. First match wins, so specific rules must come
# before wildcards. Free-tier Pages allows 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules;
# this file uses well under that.

# --- Posts that exist on both sites -----------------------------------------
/10-minutes-is-all-it-takes/  /posts/10-minutes-is-all-it-takes/  301
/start-with-your-audience/  /posts/start-with-your-audience/  301
/the-top-3-strategies-for-your-business-to-survive-and-thrive-in-the-new-digital-economy/  /posts/top-3-strategies-digital-economy/  301

